Description: pvr: advertise dualSrcBlend
 PowerVR blends in the fragment shader with nir_lower_blend(), and
 nir_lower_blend() already handles dual-source blending: consume_dual_stores()
 takes the store_output with dual_source_blend_index = 1 as the second source
 for the SRC1 blend factors and removes it. The output variable with index 1
 that nir_unlower_io_to_vars() recreated is then left without stores; remove
 it after nir_lower_blend() so that the PFO lowering and the output setup in
 pvr_setup_fs_outputs() only see the variable with index 0 at FRAG_RESULT_DATA0.
 Advertise dualSrcBlend with maxFragmentDualSrcAttachments = 1.
 .
 zink exposes GL_ARB_blend_func_extended from dualSrcBlend
 (zink_screen.c max_dual_source_render_targets), which is one of the two
 extensions missing for OpenGL 3.3.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
